WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
Hull, 2017.

2
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.510
For one year, it was UK City of Culture.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.350
New venues opened, old
ones were redeveloped,

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.690
and a gallery set out to
support local artists.

5
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.690
Five years earlier, London used sport.

6
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.570
The 2012 Games targeted East London,
one of the city's most deprived areas at

7
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.630
the time.

8
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.270
So why would a city spend
millions on a year of art?

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.210
And who decides what a place should mean?

10
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.150
In this mission, you'll
meet the governments,

11
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.590
companies and community groups who
all try to shape a place's meaning.

12
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.970
Then you'll open Hull's scorecard, and
judge what its year of culture actually

13
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.150
changed.

14
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.750
Your mission: find out why
cities pay for culture or sport,

15
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.360
and whether it works.
